Hi Shiva,

I am trying to connect Spark cluster (linux) from Windows R Shell and getting following error.
Error in .jcall(getJRDD(rdd), "Ljava/util/List;", "collect") : org.apache.hadoop.ipc.RemoteException: Server IPC version 9 cannot communicate with client version 4

I know there is hadoop version mismatch between server and client but don't know how to set correct version of my client through R code.

Following are my cluster configuration and the steps used to access it from windows,
Cluster:
SparkR build using SPARK_HADOOP_VERSION ?= 2.4.1, SPARK_VERSION ?= 1.1.0

Windows:
SparkR from http://www.cs.berkeley.edu/~shivaram/sparkr-bin/windows/SparkR_0.1.zip
installed it in to R and loading using library(SparkR).

My code:
library(SparkR)
Initialize Spark context
sc <- sparkR.init(master="local", "testFromWinds")
Read data from local File System to RDD
linesData <- textFile(sc, "Path to file test.csv", 1)
Read RDD partiions and convert each partition to matrix
dtpoints <- cache(lapplyPartition(linesData, function(part) { part = strsplit(part, ",", fixed = T) list(t(sapply(part, unlist))) }

)
)
Count of partitions
dtcnt = count(dtpoints)

When I run my r code by setting spark context to local it is working fine.
But when set Spark context to master URL like "sc <- sparkR.init(master="Master URL", "testFromWinds")" getting above error.

Please let me know if I am doing anything wrong. Any help is appreciable.

Best,
Nilesh

