Nilesh Patil <https://sparkr.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=NSP> I think the Windows binary build was built for Hadoop version 1.0.4 and Spark version 1.1.0. Thus you see the IPC version mismatch exceptions. You'll need to use a Windows package built for Hadoop 2.4.1 in this case.

You can try to build SparkR from source on Windows using the instructions at https://github.com/amplab-extras/SparkR-pkg/blob/master/BUILDING.md with the Hadoop version set to 2.4.1. Longer term we could have binary versions for commonly used Hadoop versions.

